      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "There are many more students with asthma attending public schools than previously known and documented. The challenge to identify and educate students remains largely with local school districts. A student's academic success is impacted by thorough planning and provision for the student's needs. Collecting and measuring asthma-related absence data can help drive program planning and impact school budgets."},
